<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mihailo I of Duklja</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1081</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Michael I of Duklja</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mihailo I was ruler of Duklja from about 1050 to 1081, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-vojislav">Stefan Vojislav</a>. He extended his authority over Raška, Travunia and Zachlumia and supported the Bulgarian uprising of 1072. In 1077 he received a royal crown from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-vii">Pope Gregory VII</a>, becoming the first King of Duklja. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-bodin">Constantine Bodin</a> succeeded him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mihailo-i-of-duklja.jpg" alt="Mihailo I of Duklja" width="320" height="387" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Srpski_kralj_Mihajlo_lik.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
